      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their cited evidence. The measurable claim linking declining police confidence to the accountability model is slightly inferential (the quote doesn't assert causation, and neither does the claim as stated \u2014 it says 'has not sustained trust' which is a reasonable reading). The stated-tier claim from E36 is actually from the House of Commons Library, not the policy text, but is correctly labelled 'stated' in the sense of a stated fact about legislative status \u2014 minor labelling ambiguity but not blocking. The mixed direction is genuinely supported by claims on both sides (loss of direct mandate vs. low engagement with existing model). Advocacy/interest sources (matthewbarber.co.uk, APCC) are used for projected concerns and are labelled as critics, not as sole basis for direction. No party identity or motive attribution detected. Magnitude of minor is defensible given this is a governance restructuring without direct change to legal rights. No blocking issues found."
